---
description: FocusFlow product and repository rules
alwaysApply: true
---

FocusFlow is one account and one Task across web, API, and the future extension. Canonical flow: Create Task, Prioritize, Schedule, Focus, Block Distractions, Complete Task, Analyze Results.

Phase 5e is shipped: an unconfigured assistant seam. `POST /api/assistant` uses the session user and returns not-configured. `ASSISTANT_PROVIDER` is optional and is not required at startup. Do not call an external model or add an API key unless the task says so. Phase 5d packaging remains: production Dockerfiles for the API and web app, plus a Compose file that starts Postgres, the API, and the web app. The dev Postgres Compose file still works. Images must not contain secrets. The web app proxies `/api` with `NUXT_API_PROXY_TARGET`. Production boot refuses an empty or placeholder `SESSION_SECRET`. There is no notification inbox and no Redis. Apache ECharts is used on `/analytics` only. Do not build recurring tasks unless the task says so. Keep the legacy blocker in `src/` intact. An active focus session still turns block rules on. Otherwise each rule follows its schedule.

Import task status and priority from `@focusflow/shared-types`. Derive Eisenhower quadrant from `isUrgent` and `isImportant`. Do not store quadrant.

Never trust a client userId. Scope every user-owned query by the session user.

Preserve `src/` (Website Blocker) and `mobile/` (Expo). Do not commit secrets or production mock data.

After a change, update `docs/CURSOR_CONTEXT.md`, `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md`, `docs/CHANGELOG.md`, `docs/TASKS.md`, and `docs/KNOWN_ISSUES.md` when status changed.
